## Hints

- E2: reuse day-3 `ols_fit` (rewrite it here — rebuild, don't import
  between notebooks; the repetition is the training). Regimes in (b):
  make variance depend on TIME, not on m — you want A4 broken but A2
  intact. In (c) an AR(1) error keeps E[ε|m] = 0. In (d), h = ρ·m +
  √(1−ρ²)·z with the same variance as m is the clean generator.
- E3: plim β̂ = β + γ·cov(m,h)/var(m) where γ is the omitted
  coefficient: 0.5·0.7 = 0.35 of extra slope if var(m)=var(h).
- E4(i): order by date, not by |e| — the question is whether the
  variance was constant ACROSS TIME. Vol quintiles constructed from
  rolling |r| work too.
